# Agent code

- Guest-facing turns go through `Session.ask`. That resets orchestrator counters and passes `guest_id` / `room` from the app.
- Approval uses `interrupt()` inside `safety/approval.py`. Resume with `Command(resume={"approved": bool})`.
- A node that calls `interrupt()` restarts on resume. Keep previews free of writes so the replay is safe.
- MCP calls go through `mcp_client.mcp_call`. Do not import commit functions into the model tool list.
- Live model calls use Amazon Bedrock (`HOSTEL_MODEL=bedrock`). `scripted` is only for pytest and saved traces.
- Catch tool failures at the MCP boundary and return `{status, message}`. Re-raise `GraphInterrupt`.
